Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.97,0:00:05.59,Italics_top,Ferdinand; Narration,0,0,0,,In the end, Rosemyne accepted four \Nchildren into the monastery in Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.30,0:00:07.74,Italics_top,Ferdinand; Narration,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.74,0:00:11.59,Italics_top,Ferdinand; Narration,0,0,0,,the mayor of Hasse, who was planning\Nto sell those children to the nobility,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.59,0:00:14.67,Italics_top,Ferdinand; Narration,0,0,0,,did not look kindly upon Rosemyne.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.81,0:00:20.67,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,We received quite a cold \Nreception in Hasse...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.67,0:00:22.61,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,You knew about this, didn't you, Benno?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.76,0:00:27.59,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Yes. This is precisely the kind of \Ntreatment one would expect from Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.15,0:00:53.54,Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(3000,1)}Ascendance of a Bookworm:\N{\fs20\c&HB99F4D&}Adopted Daughter of an Archduke
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.98,0:02:10.99,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,Episode 8\NFerdinand's Task
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.99,0:02:20.99,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The mayor of Hasse holds considerable \Ninfluence over the entire region.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.87,0:02:25.18,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,The territory of Ehrenfest is \Ndivided into two types of land:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.18,0:02:28.64,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,regions managed by the land-owning \Nnobles known as Giebes,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.64,0:02:30.60,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,and domains directly governed by the Aub.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.76,0:02:34.00,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Hasse is one of the directly governed \Ndomains and has been entrusted
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.00,0:02:36.71,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,with the administration of the \Nsurrounding farming villages, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.33,0:02:39.94,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,A great number of people gather
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.94,0:02:43.01,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,at the winter mansion in Hasse \Nto make it through the winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.26,0:02:47.55,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The town mayor is the one who \Ncontrols that winter mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.89,0:02:52.91,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I find it hard to believe he would \Ngrow so arrogant based on that alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.23,0:02:57.91,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,What I wish to know is what \Nkind of noble backer he has.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.15,0:03:01.18,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Judging by his demeanor toward\Nus, a party involved with
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.18,0:03:03.93,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,a major industry of Ehrenfest,\Nwhen we visited for our inspection...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.35,0:03:07.66,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,I believe he has connections with \Na noble of a very high rank.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.78,0:03:12.80,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Hmm. I am certain that the former \Nhigh bishop was one of his backers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.80,0:03:13.79,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.29,0:03:17.07,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The previous high bishop \Ndid not have a highbeast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.62,0:03:21.15,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,His movements would have been restricted \Nto areas accessible by carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.92,0:03:24.79,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,He probably flaunted his status as
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.79,0:03:27.24,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,the archduke's uncle\Nto do whatever he pleased.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.68,0:03:29.59,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Above all, their methods\N are strikingly similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.93,0:03:35.56,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,How can he remain so arrogant after \Nthe high bishop has been apprehended?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.20,0:03:39.25,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Perhaps he's unaware the \Nhigh bishop was imprisoned?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.25,0:03:41.40,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,His understanding of your \Nstatus is still likely...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.91,0:03:44.05,Flashback,Mayor,0,0,0,,Huh? That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.05,0:03:47.34,Flashback,Mayor,0,0,0,,Isn't that the blue priest that came \Nto the Spring Prayer last year?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.34,0:03:51.07,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Then, he isn't even aware that I've \Nbeen adopted by the archduke?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.39,0:03:53.34,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.34,0:03:56.04,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Benno, what kind of rumors \Nhave been circulating
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.04,0:03:58.60,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,in the lower city regarding \Nthe former high bishop?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.60,0:03:59.78,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,There aren't any.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.78,0:04:01.46,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,There have been rumors that
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.46,0:04:05.79,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,the new high bishop is a saint\Nthat can bestow real blessings,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.79,0:04:08.36,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,but everyone just assumed the \Nformer high bishop retired
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.36,0:04:09.96,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,and haven't given it much thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.74,0:04:16.73,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,That's why I said that Project \NSaint was taking things too far...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.31,0:04:23.74,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Even after his death, he \Ncontinues to cause trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.98,0:04:26.33,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,He's mulling over something again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.88,0:04:34.11,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,High Priest, I just felt \Nsomething strange...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.85,0:04:39.32,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It seems someone is attempting to force \Ntheir way into the monastery in Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.32,0:04:42.62,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I can feel a faint disturbance \Nof the defensive walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.38,0:04:45.46,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.52,0:04:48.44,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Come, Rosemyne.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.95,0:05:13.21,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Spiegeln.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.66,0:05:18.83,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,It's the monastery in Hasse!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.54,0:05:23.80,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Oh, there are people.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.80,0:05:27.80,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,In all likelihood, they've \Ncome to reclaim the children.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.11,0:05:29.07,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.79,0:05:33.71,Default,Man 3,0,0,0,,We know you're in there!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.71,0:05:34.69,Default,Man 2,0,0,0,,Come out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.70,0:05:37.40,Default,Man 3,0,0,0,,What the heck are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.41,0:05:42.02,Default,Man 1,0,0,0,,Leave this to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.00,0:05:44.57,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.26,0:05:51.03,Default,Man 1,0,0,0,,What the hell is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.09,0:05:57.84,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It seems the defensive magic \Nis working without any issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.84,0:05:59.71,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Defensive magic?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.89,0:06:00.68,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.09,0:06:04.21,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Didn't you infuse mana into the \Nfeystones of the monastery?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.22,0:06:09.98,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Oh, back then...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.23,0:06:12.04,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The defensive magic used
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.04,0:06:15.34,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,is similar to the kind you used\Nwhen you were being attacked.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.72,0:06:17.09,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,The shield of wind!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.76,0:06:22.19,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,It prevents anyone bearing ill will\N toward those inside from entering.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.12,0:06:26.28,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Well, that's a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.28,0:06:29.81,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Let's take this chance to \Ncheck on Nora and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.54,0:06:31.98,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Not right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.98,0:06:36.19,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,If we aren't careful, the mayor \Nwill be silenced like Wolf was.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.05,0:06:43.74,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,People involved with me are \Nkilled without my knowledge...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.42,0:06:47.39,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I would hate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.39,0:06:48.32,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.68,0:06:51.49,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It seems this man holds a great \Ndeal of evidence in his hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.94,0:06:54.17,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,so I would like to capture him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.28,0:06:58.78,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Do not visit Hasse until the \Nnext day of inspection.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.17,0:07:01.17,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.00,0:07:05.78,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,A few days later...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.27,0:07:10.50,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,A letter addressed to the \Nformer high bishop arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.54,0:07:18.76,Default,Mayor,0,0,0,,"One of your subordinates is behaving \Nwith the utmost arrogance."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.76,0:07:21.04,Default,Mayor,0,0,0,,"Please do something about the monastery."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.04,0:07:23.19,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Like the high priest said...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.19,0:07:26.40,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,They don't know that the \Nformer high bishop is dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.28,0:07:29.94,Default,Mayor,0,0,0,,"Even Nora, who was contracted\Nto be sold to the nobility,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.94,0:07:31.42,Default,Mayor,0,0,0,,has been snatched away from us."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.76,0:07:33.17,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,This is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.20,0:07:38.94,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It seems he doesn't know the first \Nthing about writing letters.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.16,0:07:41.47,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, Mr. Benno said...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.47,0:07:46.06,Flashback,Benno,0,0,0,,Hasse has no facilities for \Nnobles to dine or lodge in.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.32,0:07:48.50,Flashback,Benno,0,0,0,,Since it's located close \Nto the city of Ehrenfest,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.50,0:07:50.96,Flashback,Benno,0,0,0,,everyone simply passes through it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.96,0:07:53.48,Flashback,Benno,0,0,0,,Because of that, the villagers \Nhave no interaction with nobles
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.48,0:07:55.83,Flashback,Benno,0,0,0,,except for religious ceremonies \Nand tax collection.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.83,0:07:58.83,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,No wonder the mayor has \Ngotten so arrogant.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.15,0:08:02.85,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Reply that the previous high \Nbishop has passed away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.55,0:08:07.98,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I wish to confirm what he truly desires,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.98,0:08:10.98,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,a high bishop that brings\N blessings to Hasse
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.98,0:08:13.35,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,or a noble that will line his pockets?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.35,0:08:16.99,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,But doesn't this serve as \Nevidence of his misconduct?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.99,0:08:19.22,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Is it truly all right \Nto turn a blind eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.53,0:08:21.98,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,We have no choice but \Nto let him be for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.98,0:08:27.35,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It would be easy to remove him, but what \Ntruly matters is what comes after.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.35,0:08:33.73,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,But... Isn't it better to purge such \Npetty wrongdoers as soon as possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.98,0:08:37.40,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Rosemyne, what wrongdoing has he done?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.74,0:08:38.75,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.75,0:08:41.63,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Well... He sells children.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.63,0:08:43.18,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,And he's also trying to offer
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.18,0:08:45.78,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,money and valuables in \Nexchange for special favors...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.78,0:08:48.38,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,And what's wrong with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.38,0:08:49.38,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.67,0:08:52.68,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The mayor takes care of \Nthe orphaned children.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.68,0:08:55.08,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,In exchange, he holds the rights \Nof ownership over them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.08,0:08:57.46,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It is within the mayor's \Nright to sell them or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.50,0:09:02.27,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The same applies here in the \Ncathedral of Ehrenfest.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.90,0:09:08.65,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,That's right. That's the common \Nsense of this world...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.65,0:09:11.51,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Furthermore, while you call it a bribe,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.51,0:09:14.34,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,you are asking a noble to \Nmake exceptions for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.34,0:09:17.91,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Isn't it natural that you'd want \Nto make a good impression?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.40,0:09:22.59,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Didn't Benno do the very same \Nthing at our first meeting?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.97,0:09:26.40,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Back then, I was thinking of it as \Njust a token of appreciation...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.61,0:09:28.08,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,But when you put it that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.08,0:09:31.66,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I can't really explain how Benno\Nis different from the mayor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.47,0:09:33.51,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.90,0:09:36.67,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Then, the mayor hasn't \Ndone anything wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.89,0:09:38.27,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,He has.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.27,0:09:41.91,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,His crime lies in disobeying \Nthe orders of a noble like me
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.91,0:09:44.81,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,and raising an objection to our decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.74,0:09:50.94,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,So, selling children and offering \Nbribes aren't considered crimes...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.94,0:09:52.27,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.27,0:09:55.76,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,If the proceeds from selling the children,\Neven through some illicit means,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.76,0:09:58.46,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,is used to bring prosperity to the town,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.46,0:10:00.91,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,the people of Hasse will \Nstand by their mayor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.32,0:10:02.33,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.33,0:10:06.06,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Benno mentioned that even the \Nsurrounding farming villages
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.06,0:10:09.36,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,gather at the winter mansion in Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.79,0:10:12.47,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,If the townsfolk are told \Nthat he was planning
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.47,0:10:14.58,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,to use the money gained \Nfrom selling the children to nobles
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.58,0:10:17.80,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,to provide for the large number \Nof people through the winter,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.80,0:10:20.04,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,we, who selfishly snatched \Nthe children from them,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.04,0:10:22.73,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,would become the targets \Nof the townsfolk's hatred.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.22,0:10:28.86,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I know very well how vital winter \Npreparations are for commoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.27,0:10:33.10,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,When comparing the many citizens who pay \Ntheir taxes to a handful of children,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.10,0:10:35.66,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,it's obvious that priority should be \Ntaken to protect the townspeople.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.66,0:10:40.60,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,In other words, to the people \Nof Hasse, we're the villains?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.90,0:10:42.62,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,As things currently stand, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.88,0:10:44.57,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I was too naive!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.57,0:10:46.26,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I was just thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.26,0:10:49.25,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,that I could gain a workforce and those \Nchildren could gain a stable life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.70,0:10:53.24,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,That's why building a monastery seemed \Nlike such a convenient solution, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.09,0:10:58.78,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,This is what he meant \Nwhen he said not to think
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.78,0:11:00.54,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,that things would \Nconveniently go my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.11,0:11:04.42,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Since this project was approved \Nas a territory-wide initiative,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.42,0:11:08.29,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I didn't even think about\Nwhether or not it would cause
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.29,0:11:10.15,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,the people of Hasse any problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.94,0:11:13.21,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The archduke gave you \Npermission to do this because
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.21,0:11:16.75,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,he determined we would be able to collect \Ntaxes from the new laborers you create.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.27,0:11:18.71,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,This isn't a simple act of compassion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.36,0:11:23.85,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Currently, you live off of the \Ntaxes paid by the citizens.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.85,0:11:25.83,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The children and the taxpayers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.83,0:11:29.79,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Can you not tell which of the \Ntwo must be prioritized?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.98,0:11:33.24,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I understand now...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.68,0:11:37.20,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I will arrange compensation for \Nthe mayor for the children.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.20,0:11:39.80,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,That will resolve this matter, won't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.05,0:11:41.83,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.83,0:11:46.31,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,That man defied me, a noble. \NHe needs to be disposed of.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.44,0:11:50.01,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,What? But this is all my fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.01,0:11:54.69,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I never imagined our conceptions of \Nwrongdoing would be so different.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.06,0:11:56.32,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,This is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.32,0:11:59.60,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,That little bug will serve as an \Nexcellent teaching tool for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.60,0:12:04.93,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Create a faction opposing the mayor, \Nnurture it, and isolate him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.40,0:12:06.56,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Come again?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.56,0:12:10.95,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I am telling you to prepare a successor \Nthat will ensure the town of Hasse
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.95,0:12:13.72,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,will continue functioning smoothly \Nonce we remove the mayor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.03,0:12:17.97,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,If you cultivate a convenient pawn \Nthat aligns with our interests
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.97,0:12:21.22,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,before we eliminate him, things \Nwill fall neatly into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.80,0:12:23.27,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Give it a try.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.96,0:12:27.72,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,You want me to entrap someone?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.06,0:12:29.72,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Didn't I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.72,0:12:32.73,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,You must be the one to force \Nthings to go your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.10,0:12:37.83,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I grew up being taught that something \Nlike that was a bad thing to do...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.60,0:12:37.15,sfx,Text,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,450)\bord0\c&H70796D&\pos(481,66)}Morality
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.26,0:12:42.64,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,No... I'm scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.64,0:12:44.59,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I don't want to do something like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.94,0:12:46.67,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Pull yourself together.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.67,0:12:50.43,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,If you don't act, the children cannot \Nventure out into the forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.43,0:12:52.21,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,The workshop will grind to a halt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.59,0:12:56.72,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,They would become nuisances that only eat \Nthe divine blessings provided for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.68,0:12:59.87,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Surely, you didn't plan \Nto selfishly abduct them,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.87,0:13:03.60,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,lock them away, and put \Nthem into an environment
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.60,0:13:05.46,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,where they would be shunned by others?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.81,0:13:09.70,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,But... But...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.40,0:13:14.48,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I don't know how to plot against others.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.73,0:13:23.68,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It's your first time, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.68,0:13:25.53,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I will teach you how.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.00,0:13:32.76,Eyecatch_an4,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,450)}Ascendance of a\NBookworm:\N{\fs11\c&HB99F4D&}Adopted Daughter of an Archduke
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.30,0:13:39.01,Eyecatch_an6,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(450,1)}Ascendance of a\NBookworm:\N{\fs11\c&HB99F4D&}Adopted Daughter of an Archduke
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.40,0:13:42.74,Flashback,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,"Give it a try."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.13,0:13:46.00,Flashback,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,"I will teach you how."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.79,0:13:54.11,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I returned to the castle \Nfor the time being
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.11,0:13:56.89,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,to have my measurements \Ntaken for my winter attire.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.06,0:14:02.70,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,What's wrong? You look pale.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.41,0:14:07.28,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I couldn't sleep thinking about \Nthe task you gave me for Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.56,0:14:09.16,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Something as trivial as that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.10,0:14:18.67,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,You are far too weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.46,0:14:28.49,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,It may seem trivial to the high priest, \Nbut it's an impossible challenge to me...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.33,0:14:33.80,Default,Rihyarda,0,0,0,,Little princess, you look rather \Npale. Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.80,0:14:36.27,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.26,0:14:51.07,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Brother Wilfried.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.40,0:14:55.96,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,Rosemyne, you're back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.96,0:14:59.08,Default,Rihyarda,0,0,0,,Young Master, where are your attendants?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.87,0:15:03.21,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,Oh, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.21,0:15:06.21,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,M-More importantly, where \Nare you guys going?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.21,0:15:07.97,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,Are you going to see Father again?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.97,0:15:08.97,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.86,0:15:12.46,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,That's what I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.94,0:15:17.86,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,Why does Rosemyne get to see \NFather so much?! It's unfair!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.15,0:15:21.82,Default,Lamprecht,0,0,0,,Please stop, Lord Wilfried!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.76,0:15:25.22,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,I hate you! Stupid!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.96,0:15:28.72,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,You're the stupid one, Brother Wilfried!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.72,0:15:32.24,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,You're always running from your studies \Nand causing everyone around you trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.60,0:15:35.61,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I want to run away, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.61,0:15:37.16,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,But if I do...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.83,0:15:42.66,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,If you were more dependable,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.66,0:15:46.18,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I wouldn't have received such an \Nunreasonable task from Lord Ferdinand!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.49,0:15:49.50,Default,Wilfried,0,0,0,,Y-You're being too cheeky, Rosemyne!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.39,0:15:59.89,Default,Damuel,0,0,0,,Please control yourself, Lady Rosemyne!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.69,0:16:09.31,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,After that, due to the opening \Nof the Italian restaurant,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.31,0:16:13.67,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I went to my adoptive father to \Nhave him return Hugo, the chef.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.69,0:16:18.40,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,A few days later...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.53,0:16:28.03,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,It must have been scary. \NIs everyone all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.06,0:16:33.80,Default,Nora,0,0,0,,Can... May I speak?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.21,0:16:36.55,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Her speech has improved.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.55,0:16:38.34,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Her complexion, too...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.66,0:16:41.57,Default,Nora,0,0,0,,Those people weren't able to do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.57,0:16:44.81,Default,Nora,0,0,0,,I was surprised, but I also \Nfelt a sense of relief!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.81,0:16:46.04,Default,Thore,0,0,0,,Me, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.78,0:16:51.56,Default,Thore,0,0,0,,I'm glad to know that my sister \Ndefinitely can't be taken away!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.56,0:16:53.69,Default,Thore,0,0,0,,We get to eat proper meals \Nall the time, too...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.96,0:16:57.28,Default,Thore,0,0,0,,I heard from everyone that you were \Nthe one who thought of all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.28,0:16:59.94,Default,Thore,0,0,0,,Even though you're smaller than \Nme, you're pretty awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.07,0:17:04.63,Default,Marthe,0,0,0,,I'm glad we decided to come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.63,0:17:08.31,Default,Rick,0,0,0,,I'm happy just to see \NMarthe smiling again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.31,0:17:10.58,Default,Rick,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lady Rosemyne.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.50,0:17:14.93,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,The way I did things may have been wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.93,0:17:18.12,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,but it wasn't wrong to \Naccept these children...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.53,0:17:23.15,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I want to find a way for \Nboth the town of Hasse
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.15,0:17:25.90,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,and these children to \Nhave a good outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.60,0:17:29.86,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,But how can I do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.35,0:17:35.99,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,What happened? You look terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.99,0:17:39.99,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Lutz, the task the high priest gave me...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.26,0:17:49.62,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,That's pretty lenient of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.62,0:17:51.83,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Lenient?! How so?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.83,0:17:54.27,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I haven't been able to \Nsleep for days now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.27,0:17:55.64,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,I'm not talking about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.64,0:17:57.39,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,I'm talking about Hasse.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.39,0:17:59.83,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,It wouldn't have been strange \Nfor the entire town of Hasse
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.83,0:18:03.58,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,to be burned to the ground the moment \Nthey attacked the monastery.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.15,0:18:07.09,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Burn the entire town of \NHasse to the ground?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.88,0:18:09.42,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The monastery is a white building
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.42,0:18:12.79,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,that the archduke established at the \Nrequest of his adopted daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.79,0:18:17.90,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Launching an attack against it is the \Nsame as attacking the archduke's family.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.27,0:18:20.28,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,What?! Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.55,0:18:23.16,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you didn't realize that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.95,0:18:25.54,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I didn't...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.54,0:18:27.58,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,You already know what happens
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.58,0:18:30.97,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,to someone who attacks a member \Nof the archduke's family, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.71,0:18:37.02,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Count Bindewald was imprisoned\N for attacking me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.02,0:18:39.54,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,the archduke's adopted daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.97,0:18:44.64,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Since even nobles are punished, there's \Nno way commoners wouldn't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.83,0:18:46.98,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.98,0:18:49.93,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,If I wasn't given this task, Hasse...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.22,0:18:52.72,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The entire town would \Nhave been long gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.72,0:18:56.99,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Hasse will be finished the moment the \Nattack becomes public knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.47,0:19:02.46,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Even merchants do things like creating \Nopposing factions to stir the pot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.46,0:19:06.09,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,It's something you'll eventually have to \Nlearn as the archduke's daughter anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.54,0:19:10.36,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,Like the high priest said, this is \Nan excellent teaching tool for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.50,0:19:15.60,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.60,0:19:19.52,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I don't want to do something \Nlike scheme and entrap someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.44,0:19:25.26,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,Then, just change your way of thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.26,0:19:26.26,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.26,0:19:28.66,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,You're not entrapping the mayor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.66,0:19:32.38,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,You're saving the people of Hasse who \Nare getting dragged into this mess
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.38,0:19:34.19,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,because of the mayor. Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.19,0:19:37.53,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I'm saving the people of Hasse...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.53,0:19:39.19,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,Yeah, you're saving them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:41.23,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,After all, the high bishop of Ehrenfest
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.23,0:19:44.52,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,is a saint who can bestow real \Ndivine blessings to others.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.99,0:19:49.54,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,If I think of it that way, \NI think I can do it...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.99,0:19:58.66,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Your complexion has improved a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.92,0:20:01.06,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,I was able to gain advice \Nfrom Lutz and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.51,0:20:04.69,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,And what of the task I gave you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.29,0:20:06.33,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.33,0:20:07.80,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,We will create rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.06,0:20:10.44,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Hm, what kind of rumors?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.61,0:20:17.55,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The monastery in Hasse was attacked \Nand now the entire town is in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.82,0:20:20.51,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,The compassionate high bishop fears
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.51,0:20:23.89,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,that even though the attackers were \Npeople related to the town mayor,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.89,0:20:27.38,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,the innocent townsfolk that have nothing \Nto do with it will be punished as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.82,0:20:30.71,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,At the same time, we will \Ncirculate another rumor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.95,0:20:33.69,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,Who is going to be held \Naccountable for the attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.69,0:20:37.77,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,Steer clear of Hasse if you want to \Navoid getting dragged into this mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.37,0:20:40.80,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,This sense of unease, along with \Ntheir fear of the nobility,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.80,0:20:43.21,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,should morph into resentment \Nagainst the mayor's faction,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.21,0:20:45.69,Default,Mark,0,0,0,,allowing us to isolate him completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.34,0:20:52.44,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,I'm a little surprised that \NMr. Mark and the high priest
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.44,0:20:54.17,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,are actually the same type of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.78,0:20:58.47,Default,Lutz,0,0,0,,The speed that rumors spread \Nby merchants is really crazy!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.99,0:21:03.37,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,In that case, we have no choice \Nbut to go through with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.37,0:21:09.04,Default,Benno,0,0,0,,However, if we spread these rumors, the \Nincident in Hasse will become public knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.36,0:21:17.74,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,A fitting plan for someone like you, \Nwho has deep ties with the lower city.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.12,0:21:19.32,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,How interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.32,0:21:20.87,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Do as you planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.18,0:21:21.99,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.38,0:21:28.08,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Even so, I can't believe you didn't even \Nrealize the meaning of attacking the monastery.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.63,0:21:32.66,Italics,Rosemyne-Internal,0,0,0,,Looks like he won't turn a \Nblind eye to that part...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.03,0:21:45.54,Creditsv2,Sign,0,0,0,,Translation   Angela Tamae Liu
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.54,0:21:53.33,Creditsv2,Sign,0,0,0,,Timing   Edgar Cruz
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.33,0:21:57.34,Creditsv2,Sign,0,0,0,,Editing   Tara Campbell
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.34,0:22:01.47,Creditsv2,Sign,0,0,0,,QC   Alicia Ashby
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.47,0:22:05.98,Creditsv2,Sign,0,0,0,,FQC   Michelle Tymon
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.03,0:23:13.03,Next_Chapter,Sign,0,0,0,,Next Episode\NWilfried's Day as High Bishop
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.03,0:23:17.53,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Why did you fail to grasp the significance\N of the attack on the monastery?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.53,0:23:19.71,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Our common sense is too different.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.71,0:23:24.29,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,Don't you understand that better than \Nanyone, since you peered into my memories?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.57,0:23:29.09,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,I recall you seemed to have \Na rather comfortable life...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.09,0:23:32.22,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,Weren't you the daughter of \Nan upper-class noble family?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.44,0:23:36.95,Default,Rosemyne,0,0,0,,There aren't any nobles in that world. \NWe don't even have a class system.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.76,0:23:42.97,Default,Ferdinand,0,0,0,,It seems I will have to reconsider your \Neducation plan from the very foundations.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.99,0:23:50.07,Illustration_by_,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(501,321)}Illustration: Kikuta Yui

